WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:14.513
As they approached Columbus' three ships, Vinnie noticed a few sickly men.

2
00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:17.564
They were very thin and pale.

3
00:00:17.565 --> 00:00:21.863
One man had dark spots on his legs.

4
00:00:21.864 --> 00:00:28.035
"Julio," Vinnie whispered. "Those men look very ill."

5
00:00:28.036 --> 00:00:30.950
Julio nodded sadly.

6
00:00:30.951 --> 00:00:34.474
"They have just gotten back from a long journey.

7
00:00:34.475 --> 00:00:36.605
They have scurvy."

8
00:00:36.606 --> 00:00:39.828
"Scurvy?" asked Vinnie.

9
00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:44.423
"It's a disease some sailors get," said Julio.

10
00:00:44.424 --> 00:00:49.402
"The ship's doctor thinks it's because sailors don't eat enough fruit."

11
00:00:49.403 --> 00:00:54.614
"But fruit is good for you!" exclaimed Mandy.

12
00:00:54.615 --> 00:00:57.385
Julio smiled at her.

13
00:00:57.386 --> 00:00:59.708
"You're right, Mandy.

14
00:00:59.709 --> 00:01:03.405
But, aboard ship, fruit rots very quickly.

15
00:01:03.406 --> 00:01:08.344
On long voyages, it's impossible to keep fruit fresh."

16
00:01:08.345 --> 00:01:12.326
Vinnie and Mandy looked at the sick men.

17
00:01:12.327 --> 00:01:16.276
"That's sad," said Mandy.

18
00:01:16.277 --> 00:01:22.774
Suddenly, a high-pitched whistle blew and the pier buzzed with excitement.

19
00:01:22.775 --> 00:01:26.276
"Time to sail," said Julio.

20
00:01:26.277 --> 00:01:30.359
"But what about the book?" Mandy asked.

21
00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.899
Julio looked around.

22
00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:37.339
Sailors were rushing past him and boarding the ships.

23
00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:40.253
"Look!" he shouted.

24
00:01:40.254 --> 00:01:45.251
"There's Columbus on the Santa Maria. Come on!"

25
00:01:45.252 --> 00:01:50.433
Julio ran onto the ship, and the children followed.

26
00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:54.467
On deck, a man stood by the ship's rail.

27
00:01:54.468 --> 00:01:58.340
He was holding several sheets of paper.

28
00:01:58.341 --> 00:02:03.019
"Julio, get to your post," ordered the man.

29
00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:08.273
"Diego, these children must see Columbus," said Julio.

30
00:02:08.274 --> 00:02:10.705
"Can you take them to him?"

31
00:02:10.706 --> 00:02:14.394
Diego looked at the children impatiently.

32
00:02:14.395 --> 00:02:17.857
"He has no time for children," he said.

33
00:02:17.858 --> 00:02:20.816
"Go away."

34
00:02:20.817 --> 00:02:24.299
"Please," pleaded Julio.

35
00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.369
"It's important that they see the captain.

36
00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:31.918
This little girl found his book and wants to give it back to him."

37
00:02:31.919 --> 00:02:38.017
"Since you are Martin Alonzo's nephew, I will do as you ask," said Diego.

38
00:02:38.018 --> 00:02:40.716
"Good-bye, Vinnie and Mandy.

39
00:02:40.717 --> 00:02:44.640
It was nice meeting you," said Julio.

40
00:02:44.641 --> 00:02:49.551
He waved before running off to another part of the ship.

41
00:02:49.552 --> 00:02:54.253
"Thank you, Julio!" cried the children.

42
00:02:54.254 --> 00:02:58.741
"Come on, we're sailing in a few minutes," said Diego.

43
00:02:58.742 --> 00:03:03.146
He led them past sailors getting the ship ready.

44
00:03:03.147 --> 00:03:09.374
"I can't believe we're on the Santa Maria!" gasped Vinnie.

45
00:03:09.375 --> 00:03:12.374
He looked around excitedly.

46
00:03:12.375 --> 00:03:18.245
Mandy noticed some men carrying big sacks to an opening in the deck.

47
00:03:18.246 --> 00:03:22.323
A ladder led down into the cargo hold.

48
00:03:22.324 --> 00:03:26.886
With a loud crash, one of the men dropped a sack.

49
00:03:26.887 --> 00:03:31.313
Potatoes spilled out, all over the deck.

50
00:03:31.314 --> 00:03:37.630
"Watch out!" shouted Diego. "Grab those potatoes!"

51
00:03:37.631 --> 00:03:42.360
Everyone stopped to catch the rolling potatoes.

52
00:03:42.361 --> 00:03:46.524
"I got one!" Mandy shouted.

53
00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:48.073
"I'll get that one,"

54
00:03:48.074 --> 00:03:55.069
Vinnie called, running after a potato that rolled a long way down the deck.

55
00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:59.254
Soon the potatoes were collected in the sack again.

56
00:03:59.255 --> 00:04:03.956
A young boy stepped forward and tied the sack tight.

57
00:04:03.957 --> 00:04:07.883
Mandy wiped her hands on her skirt.

58
00:04:07.884 --> 00:04:12.122
"That was fun," she said, laughing.

59
00:04:12.123 --> 00:04:14.312
Then she stopped.

60
00:04:14.313 --> 00:04:17.683
"Vinnie! The ship is moving!"

61
00:04:17.684 --> 00:04:22.656
Mandy looked around, but could not see her brother.

62
00:04:22.657 --> 00:04:26.776
Vinnie had disappeared into the crowd of sailors.

63
00:04:26.777 --> 00:04:31.617
The Santa Maria was pulling slowly away from the pier.

64
00:04:31.618 --> 00:04:41.321
"Oh no! What am I going to do?" she said to herself.
